Yes. The important thing is to understand **what each `WebElement` method is actually checking/doing**, and especially the difference between `isDisplayed()`, `isEnabled()`, `isSelected()`, and Selenium's `click()` behavior.

## `WebElement` methods — when to use each

| Method           | What it does                                  | Common use                              |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `sendKeys()`     | Types text / sends keyboard input             | Text boxes, file upload                 |
| `click()`        | Clicks an element                             | Button, checkbox, radio, link           |
| `clear()`        | Removes existing text                         | Input/text area                         |
| `getText()`      | Gets visible text inside an element           | Labels, headings, buttons, `<div>`      |
| `getAttribute()` | Gets an HTML attribute/property value         | `value`, `href`, `placeholder`, `class` |
| `isDisplayed()`  | Checks whether element is visible             | Visibility assertion                    |
| `isEnabled()`    | Checks whether element can be interacted with | Disabled/enabled button                 |
| `isSelected()`   | Checks selected state                         | Checkbox/radio/select option            |

