# Easy way to remember all 8

```text
ACTION
│
├── sendKeys()       → Type
├── click()          → Click
└── clear()          → Remove text
```

```text
READ / VERIFY
│
├── getText()        → Visible text
├── getAttribute()   → Attribute/property value
│
├── isDisplayed()    → Visible?
├── isEnabled()      → Enabled?
└── isSelected()     → Selected?
```

### For your DemoQA form

```java
firstName.sendKeys("Jaswanth");       // ACTION

firstName.clear();                    // ACTION

submit.click();                       // ACTION

heading.getText();                    // READ TEXT

firstName.getAttribute("value");      // READ INPUT VALUE

firstName.isDisplayed();              // VERIFY VISIBILITY

submit.isEnabled();                   // VERIFY ENABLED

male.isSelected();                    // VERIFY RADIO
```

The big distinction to remember is:

**`isDisplayed()` = "Can I see it?"**
**`isEnabled()` = "Is it enabled?"**
**`isSelected()` = "Is it selected?"**
**None of these forces an interaction.**

